{
  "case_id": "2009-08-661",
  "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court of Appeals for the\nSeventh Circuit held that an agreement of the 32 teams\nof the National Football League was immune from any\nscrutiny under section 1 of the Sherman Act on the\nground that the agreement allegedly fails the\nplurality of actor requirement of this Court's\njurisprudence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But there was no joint\nventure with respect to the television rights, meaning\nthere was no separate activity, other than the\ntelevising of the shows at issue. Here, the Solicitor\nGeneral is saying there is a joint venture, and it has\nto do with the licensing of trademarks, with their\nquality control, et cetera.\nIsn't that a substantial difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, too, here, the 32 teams of the National Football League have entered into an agreement and control the use, collectively, of the trademarks and logos of the individual teams. And for that reason, there is concerted activity that is involved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nager",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the only question before the Court is whether or not these agreements constitute concerted activity. They plainly do, because they are agreements between separately owned and controlled competing businesses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, could you articulate for me as succinctly as possible the extent to which your position departs from the position of the Solicitor General?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And one thing I wondered about the record: There is discussion in the briefs about the fact that the teams share the revenues from these -- these sales. Is that -- how did that get in the record, the revenue sharing aspect of their -- of the different teams' participation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Malcolm L. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0001-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that follows logically from the position that this is one entity. Because in Copperweld, for instance, the Court noted that coordination between different divisions of a single company would not be subject to section 1 scrutiny, and that implies not just that all the divisions could get together, but that any two could confer among themselves without raising section 1 concerns."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, do we have to ask what was the intent at the beginning, as kind of an originalism thing? Everybody sits around and says: Let's have a football league. And 20 years later, they say: You know, the sale of hats and shirts is a pretty good thing; let's get into that business, too. That would -- that would -- that's case 1."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Levy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEVY: Your Honor, we know here that at least as of 1963, when NFL Properties was formed, that there was a single entity formed, a single entity to produce and promote NFL football."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Levy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEVY: I'm not suggesting that the original agreement is sacrosanct. That's why I suggested that by 1963 -- or the mid-1960s, when NFL Properties was formed, there was venture formation at that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May -- may I ask you to go back just one step? Because you seem to treat this as though the NFLP was formed in 1963 and that was the end of it, but another description is: Well, it was formed, but then there were some teams that were not in it until later, and there were some other parts, that it has expanded. What it does has expanded since 1963."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. Did the teams -- did the NFL Properties or some centralized entity always exploit the trademarks of all the franchises, or was there a long period of time in which they each individually franchised their products?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What decision could the sports teams make that would be subject to the antitrust scrutiny under your definition of the permissible range of the joint venture activities? It seems to me that if the venture wanted to make sure all the teams hired secretaries at the same $1,000-a-year salary, that under your theory, that's okay, because it's a joint venture."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- if the reasonableness of this decision, that T-shirts promote the game, is so self-evident, then why wouldn't the rule of reason control completely?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Needle",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The answer, Your Honor, is inherent in the rule of reason. In the modern era, defending a claim like this on the merits involves an investment of tens of millions of dollars, thousands of hours of executive time, hours and hours of court time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's the need to -- to label it \u201csingle entity,\u201d as opposed to label it what it is, reasonable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you -- you say that the -- that the trademarks have no value apart from the -- from the game. I guess you could say the same thing for each individual franchise of each of the 32 clubs. They are worthless, if NFL football disappears."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a0807576b65d99f3e7e864c65b9d57a47ca5b5a9a8065d88837669b962e5802",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a0807576b65-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:19 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
